{
  "dom_id": "step-q339283",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\pi /{3}^{+}}({cos}^{2}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /{3}^{+}}({cos}^{2}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) & ={cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
